From eac4920ef52236526e67fc3d82b7ccd406a38cd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d00f <8052722+DrDoof@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/20] boot: start the second and the SFP poll when the main
 loop starts

Both timers were set before the reset button was handled at boot. A
button held for the whole 30 s of that handler left the second timer
that far behind, and the main loop then caught up one second per tick:
the first of those seconds saw the button pressed, the next ones
advanced the seconds counter, and the release measured more than ten
seconds and reverted the configuration. The old 8-bit tick count wrapped
before that could happen.
---
